## PROGRESSIVE DOCUMENTATION v2 (v1.7.0 — MANDATORY CONTRACT)

> **Why this exists:** In v1.6.0 and earlier, all file writes happened at Phase 5+. By Phase 6, context windows were near-exhausted, and the agent had to *regenerate from chat memory* — losing fidelity. v1.7.0 reverses this: **every phase that produces content writes to the corresponding section before its checkpoint.** Phase 6 is then a *consolidate-and-polish* pass over progressively-built sections, not a from-scratch generation. This is the TDA pattern (`r-genie/01_Technical_Design_Agent/rules/01-01_Phase_Orchestration.mdc`) adapted to the 9-phase CSA workflow. Critical Rule #16 in `Cloud_Success_Architect.mdc` is the binding enforcement.

### Per-Phase Write Contract

| Phase | Writes to `HLD.md` section | Writes to `Supporting.md` section | Other artifact writes |
|-------|-----------------------------------|------------------------------------------|------------------------|
| **0 — Intake** | _(SKELETON)_ create file from `templates/HLD-template.md` with all `<!-- SECTION: ... -->` placeholders | _(SKELETON)_ create file from `templates/Supporting-Doc-template.md` with all `<!-- SECTION: ... -->` placeholders | _(none yet)_ |
| **1 — Problem Deep-Dive** | §3 What We Heard (persona quotes) | §1.2 Business Drivers + Top Pains (full evidence) | _(none)_ |
| **2A — Current State** | _(none — too early for narrative)_ | §3 Current State Snapshot (footprint table) | _(none)_ |
| **2B — Live Research** | §2 Why Now (3-row forces table — research-informed) | §3 (extend with research findings) | `research_log.md` |
| **3 — ToT Brainstorming** | _(none — branches don't enter HLD)_ | §2 Design Rationale §2.1 Branches + §2.2 Tradeoff Matrix | _(none)_ |
| **4 prelim** | _(none — component list is internal)_ | §2 §2.3 Component Draft List | _(none)_ |
| **4A — Feasibility** | _(none — depth lives in Supporting)_ | §3.5 Feasibility Validation Matrix (full 8-dim) | _(none)_ |
| **4B — Coverage** | §6.5 How This Solves Your Problems (panel-friendly subset) | Appendix A Coverage Matrix (full bidirectional) | _(none)_ |
| **4C — KPIs** | §11 Success Metrics & KPIs (3-tier table) | §10 Measurement & Observability (skeleton + per-KPI rows) | _(may produce stub `KPI_Baselines_v1.md` early)_ |
| **5 — Persona Refinement** | _APPEND DELTAS ONLY_ to §3 / §6.5 / §11 if Phase 5 OPPs touch them (audit trail in Refinement Log) | _APPEND DELTAS ONLY_ to §3.5 / §10 / Appendix A if Phase 4 deltas re-validate | `Refinement_Log.md` (full per-persona log) |
| **6 — HLD Consolidate** | §1 Executive Summary · §4 Future State · §5 Architecture (Mermaid) · §6 Design Choices · §7 Data Flows (text summary) · §8 Accelerators · §9 Roadmap · §10 Your Ask — and POLISH §3 / §6.5 / §11 | _(no Supporting writes — that's Phase 7)_ | **`diagrams.md`** (per-flow drill-downs — mandatory if ≥2 capability flows) |
| **7 — Supporting Consolidate** | _(no HLD writes — locked at Phase 6)_ | §1 Reviewer Summary · §2 Design Rationale (Components) · §4 Risk Register · §4.5 NFR Compliance · §5 Assumption Log · §6 Gap Register · §7 Phased Roadmap · §8 Talk Track · §9 Cross-Ref · POLISH §3 / §3.5 / §10 / Appendix A / Appendix B | `KPI_Baselines_v1.md` (final signed-off version) |
| **8 — Panel Prep** | _(no edits — HLD/Supporting are locked)_ | _(no edits)_ | `Panel_QA.md` |

### Per-Phase Write Protocol (the TDA pattern adapted)

For EVERY phase that has writes per the contract above:

1. **PRESENT analytical content in chat** — tables, decisions, branches, matrices — per phase task list
2. **GET user approval** at the phase checkpoint
3. **SHOW preview** of what will be written to file (1-3 lines of compressed prose) — confirm the structural budget per `templates/HLD-template.md` is met
4. **WRITE clean content** to the corresponding `<!-- SECTION: X -->` marker via `edit`/`multi_edit` (NOT a full file regeneration)
5. **VERIFY the write** by re-reading the section markers — confirm content landed in the right place
6. **UPDATE state file** `phaseStatuses.phaseN.status = "COMPLETED"` AND `generatedArtifacts[]` entry for the file (size, lines, sections-now-filled)
7. **ONLY THEN** present next-phase prompt

**Forbidden after Phase 0:** chat-only intermediate output. Every analytical artifact (problem deep-dive, capability scan, ToT branches, feasibility matrix, coverage matrix, KPI table) MUST persist to file before its checkpoint approval is accepted. This is the binding rule that prevents Gap #2 (context-window exhaustion).

**Conciseness during progressive writes (v1.7.0):** Each section's structural budget (per `templates/HLD-template.md`) is the binding constraint. Total HLD line count is a **soft signal** with advisory threshold ~380 lines (2× retail example). Forbidden Phrases (`@02_Mandatory_Stop_Points.mdc`) remain the primary anti-verbosity enforcement. The hard 250-line cap from v1.5.0/v1.6.0 is **superseded** — see Production Learning #1.2 for rationale.

### Phase 6 Consolidate-Mode (Critical Redefinition)

Phase 6 is NO LONGER a from-scratch HLD generation. It is a **consolidate-and-polish** pass:

1. **READ** the progressively-built HLD (§3 from Phase 1, §2 from Phase 2B, §6.5 from Phase 4B, §11 from Phase 4C, plus any Phase 5 deltas)
2. **GENERATE** the missing sections in order: §1 Exec Summary (now everything is known) → §4 Future State table → §5 Proposed Architecture Mermaid + 5-bullet description → §6 Design Choices (3-5 choices, 3-bullet format each) → §7 Data Flows text summary → §8 Accelerators → §9 Roadmap → §10 Your Ask
3. **PRODUCE `diagrams.md`** from `templates/diagrams-template.md` if the architecture has ≥2 distinct capability flows (cap 4; defer remainder to Supporting Doc Appendix C). Apply Per-Flow Drill-Down recipe from `01_Guidance.mdc` §7.7.2.
4. **POLISH** the progressively-built sections (§3, §6.5, §11) for verbosity discipline + Forbidden Phrases sweep
5. **VERIFY** structural budgets met per section + diagram syntax (`<br/>`, `curve: linear`, layout order, edge semantics, no dangling nodes — `01_Guidance.mdc` §7.6 D1-D8)

The context-window benefit: by Phase 6, the agent has 4 sections already written and 6 sections to generate (instead of generating all 10 from scratch). The 6 generation tasks are individually small (per-section budgets in template). This survives long sessions.

