## PHASE 6: HLD CONSOLIDATE & POLISH + PER-FLOW DIAGRAMS (Progressive Documentation v2)

> **v1.7.0 CRITICAL REDEFINITION:** Phase 6 is **consolidate-and-polish**, NOT from-scratch generation. By this phase, `HLD.md` already contains §3 (Phase 1), §2 (Phase 2B), §6.5 (Phase 4B), §11 (Phase 4C), and any Phase 5 deltas. Phase 6 generates the **6 remaining sections** + the per-flow drill-downs artifact, then polishes the whole document.

**Phase 6 Task List (7 steps):**

**Step 1 — RE-READ progressively-built HLD.** Confirm §2, §3, §6.5, §11 are present and updated with Phase 5 deltas. List which `<!-- SECTION: X -->` markers are still placeholders.

**Step 2 — Generate §1 Executive Summary.** Now that the full solution is locked, write ≤80 words / 3 sentences: (S1) who you are + one stated pain quoted; (S2) what we propose in 12-18 words; (S3) the measured outcome at 12 months.

**Step 3 — Generate §4 Aspirational Future State.** ≤5-row table mapping Today (from Phase 1 facts) → 12-18 Months From Now (from ambition) → Stakeholder Who Cares.

**Step 4 — Generate §5 Proposed Architecture.** ONE Mermaid `flowchart LR` diagram ≤12 primary nodes following recipe `01_Guidance.mdc` §7.7.1 (Architecture-HLD): subgraph dashed-borders + 4-class OR 18-class palette + action `-->` vs governance `-.->` edges. Apply ALL 8 syntax/layout rules from §7.6 D1-D8. Follow with the 5-bullet "How this works for you" block (≤25 words each).

**Step 5 — Generate §6 Design Choices + §7 Data Flows summary.** §6 = 3-5 design choices in 3-bullet format (What/Why for you/Business benefit, each ≤30 words). §7 = max 2 flows as text summaries (each ≤8 numbered steps, ≤15 words/step) — cross-referencing `diagrams.md` for visuals.

**Step 6 — Generate §8 Accelerators + §9 Roadmap + §10 Your Ask.** §8 = ≤6-row accelerator table. §9 = 90/180/365-day horizon table. §10 = 3 time-boxed asks + 2-3 commitments-in-return.

**Step 7 — Produce `diagrams.md`** _(NEW in v1.7.0)_:
   - **Decision:** if `finalist.capabilityFlows[].length >= 2` per state, this artifact is **mandatory**. If <2, **skip** (HLD §7 text summary suffices).
   - **Create** `diagrams.md` from `templates/diagrams-template.md`
   - **Generate** 1 Mermaid drill-down per capability flow (cap **4 flows**; defer remainder to Supporting Doc Appendix C)
   - **Apply** Per-Flow Drill-Down recipe `01_Guidance.mdc` §7.7.2: init directive merging `curve: linear` + `themeVariables.fontSize: 16px`; numbered-step labels on edges ("1. Action ≤8 words"); subgraphs by logical zone (Data Sources / MuleSoft API-Led / Salesforce Platform / Backend); 4-class minimal palette (`sf` / `ms` / `backend` / `user`) per recipe §7.7.1
   - **Add** "Strategy Summary" 3-4 bullets per flow (architectural rationale, NOT narrative)

**Step 8 — POLISH the progressively-built sections** (§3 quotes, §6.5 coverage, §11 KPIs) — Forbidden Phrases sweep + structural budget verification + Mermaid syntax check D1-D8.

**Step 9 — Update generation footer** of HLD: `Authored with: Cloud Success Architect Agent v1.7.0 | {generation-date}`.

> HLD audience is the **panel**. Write in "you" terms. No deep technical jargon. Diagrams > paragraphs. Use Solution **v2** (Phase 5 exit), not v1. See `templates/HLD-template.md` for canonical structure. **Conciseness is example-anchored** — benchmark against `examples/retail-personalized-offerings_HLD.md` (~190 lines for a 4-capability use case). Total HLD line count is a *soft signal* with advisory threshold ~380 lines.

**RGV Cycle:** READ progressively-built HLD sections (4 already filled: §2, §3, §6.5, §11) + Solution v2 components (N) + Phase 4B+5 coverage matrix + Phase 4C+5 KPIs + pains (M) + personas + `finalist.capabilityFlows[]` count → GENERATE 6 remaining HLD sections (§1, §4, §5, §6, §7, §8-§10) + `diagrams.md` (if ≥2 flows) → VERIFY: every component cited with customer fact, all personas addressed, "you" language throughout, §6.5 reflects all Phase 5 deltas, §11 has every KPI with Baseline+Target+Window+Owner, `diagrams.md` has 1 Mermaid per capability flow with recipe §7.7.2 applied, syntax D1-D8 passes → FIX any "they/the customer" → "you", complete remaining sections, `<br/>` discipline applied to all node/edge labels.

**Checkpoint 6:** HLD consolidated (all 10+ sections filled with verbosity discipline) + `diagrams.md` produced (if applicable) + all Forbidden Phrases gates pass. Ask user to review in IDE. STOP.

