## EXECUTION RULES, RGV, CONFIDENCE & FORENSIC PROTOCOL

**Per-phase rhythm:** **Before:** load relevant `@01_Guidance.mdc` section + produce `<thinking>` block + assess Confidence. **During:** follow phase tasks + apply RGV for generation phases (3, 5, 6, 7, 8) + cite evidence. **After:** present checkpoint, STOP and WAIT, update state file on approval.

**Confidence levels:** HIGH (clear customer facts, proven capability) → proceed. MEDIUM (partial context, reasonable inference) → flag `⚠️ ASSUMPTION`, recommend validation. LOW (vague/contradictory) → STOP, request clarification.

**RGV pattern:** READ (inputs from prior phases — count/list) → GENERATE (artifact sections — count/list) → VERIFY ("Grounded X/Y sections with citations") → FIX (any ungrounded) before checkpoint. **If X ≠ Y, do NOT present the checkpoint.**

**Forensic Input Processing (Phase 0):** (1) INVENTORY = mind map (sections + numerical anchors); (2) SECTION-BY-SECTION RGV; (3) POSITIONAL BIAS SCAN — re-read 30%–70% (LLMs under-index middles); (4) COMPLETENESS VERIFICATION (>10% delta → re-read); (5) CROSS-SECTION COHERENCE — flag contradictions.

---

## RESUME, BACKWARD NAVIGATION & ERROR RECOVERY

**Resume:** on activation, check for `project/output_cloud_success_architect/{slug}/.success-architect-state.json` → show last completed phase, offer resume/restart. Multiple slugs → ask which.

**Backward navigation:** "revise phase N" → mark N+1…8 `NEEDS_REVIEW`. Special cases: "switch finalist" → re-run 4A+4B+4C+5; "re-run feasibility" → 4B/4C/5-8; "re-run coverage" → 4C/5-8; "revise KPIs" → 5-8; "re-run refinement" → re-engage Phase 5 with current solution; "edition/entitlement changed" → re-check 4A Edition dim, then 4B/4C/5-8. Full cascade map: `lib/docs/state-schema-reference.md` §"Backward Navigation Cascade".

**Error recovery:** mid-generation failure → save state + report + offer retry. Unreadable input → ask for paste. Conflicting customer facts → flag + ask which to trust + log decision. Disconnect → state preserved.

